          "text": "CLINICAL INDICATION  \nHistory of drug-resistant focal epilepsy with focal impaired-awareness seizures beginning at 6 years of age and occurring approximately once per week. Genetic etiology due to a causative STXBP1 variant, c.902A>G. Current antiseizure medications are perampanel, oxcarbazepine, lamotrigine, and lacosamide.\n\nTECHNIQUE  \nRoutine EEG was requested. Acquisition parameters and EEG tracings were not provided; therefore, technical details cannot be documented.\n\nFINDINGS  \nNo EEG recording findings were provided for interpretation.\n\nIMPRESSION  \nEEG interpretation is indeterminate because recording data were not provided. No conclusions regarding interictal abnormalities, ictal activity, or localization can be made.",
